From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: acm: initialize the entire stdio descriptor

With CONSOLE_FLUSH_SUPPORT, stdio_dev includes an optional flush callback.
The ACM initializer leaves it uninitialized on the stack. panic() flushes
stdout before resetting, so a console using ACM can branch into garbage
instead of resetting, recursively faulting in the exception handler.

Zero the descriptor before assigning supported callbacks. ACM has no flush
implementation, so the console should skip its NULL callback. This local
fix also initializes unused fields for configurations without flush support.
Baseline: U-Boot v2026.10-rc5, a06e89ab05eaa2b8344d521319399333cd760ae5.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_acm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_acm.c
@@ -673,7 +673,7 @@ static int acm_stdio_stop(struct stdio_dev *dev)
 
 int drv_usbacm_init(void)
 {
-	struct stdio_dev stdio;
+	struct stdio_dev stdio = { 0 };
 
 	strcpy(stdio.name, "usbacm");
 	stdio.flags = DEV_FLAGS_INPUT | DEV_FLAGS_OUTPUT;
